@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Zendesk Account Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account information transfers properly to zendesk in the form of a ticket.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Service Partnership |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Basic Reseller Partnership" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Basic Reseller Partnership |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Distribution Partnership" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Distribution Partnership |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Training Partnership" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Training Partnership |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Value-Added Reseller Partnership" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Value-Added Reseller Partnership |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Gold Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id and domain values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | salesforce |
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | dossiera   |
	| zyxwvuts0987654321            | salesforce |
	| zyxwvuts0987654321            | dossiera   |
	| ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | salesforce |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Service Partnership              |
	| Basic Reseller Partnership       |
	| Distribution Partnership         |
	| Training Partnership             |
	| Value-Added Reseller Partnership |
	| Digital Enterprise Production    |
	| Liferay DXP Production           |
	| Platinum Subscription            |
	| Gold Subscription                |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Service Partnership              |
	| Basic Reseller Partnership       |
	| Distribution Partnership         |
	| Training Partnership             |
	| Platinum Subscription            |
	| Gold Subscription                |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Customer Role |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korzen - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORZENKORZEN  |
	| KORZENKORZEN1 |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korzen - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Korzen - ${staticProjectName} |

Scenario: View new business ticket
	Testing the ability to create a new business in Dossiera and viewing the project in the form of a zendesk ticket

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay DXP Production                     |
	| Project Name                           | Korzen - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should be synced to zendesk
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the subject "New Subscription for Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the text "Account Name: Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the text "Account Code: KORZENKORZEN" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the text "Opportunity Type: New Business" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the requester with the email address "provisioningrequest@liferay.com"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the organization "Provisioning"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the product "prd_provisioning_request"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the support region "United States"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the opportunity owner "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the primary address country "United States"

Scenario: View existing business ticket
	Testing the ability to create an existing business in Dossiera and viewing the project in the form of a zendesk ticket

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORZENKORZEN                         |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Name                  | Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}        |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                  |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dossiera                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	| Entity Name | account                     |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | salesforce                    |
	| Entity Id   | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	| Entity Name | project                       |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Digital Enterprise Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay DXP Production                     |
	| Project Name                           | Korzen - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | Existing Business                          |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should be synced to zendesk
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the subject "New Subscription for Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the text "Account Name: Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the text "Account Code: KORZENKORZEN" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the text "Opportunity Type: Existing Business" in its description
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the requester with the email address "provisioningrequest@liferay.com"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the organization "Provisioning"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the product "prd_provisioning_request"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the support region "United States"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the opportunity owner "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with keywords "Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the primary address country "United States"

Scenario: View existing business ticket with notes
	Testing the ability to create an existing business with pinned notes in Dossiera and viewing the project in the form of a zendesk ticket

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORZENKORZEN                         |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Name                  | Korzen - ${staticCompanyName}        |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
